{"id": 20, "ts": 1780655512.502115, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate the thoroughness of the earlier points, but I remain concerned that we are missing critical safety\u2011related data for both Candidate\u202fA and Candidate\u202fD. While Candidate\u202fA\u2019s technical strengths (anticipating danger, complex\u2011connection insight, spatial vision, strong leadership) are impressive, we have no evidence of his stress\u2011resilience or crew\u2011cooperation under pressure\u2014both essential for long\u2011distance flights. Candidate\u202fD, despite showing strong concentration, problem\u2011solving, and responsibility, also lacks any concrete proof of handling stress or collaborating with crew in high\u2011stress scenarios, and his arrogance and weak leadership further raise doubts about crew dynamics. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC has documented strengths in crew\u2011cooperation (creates a positive atmosphere), decision\u2011making speed, and attention, even though he has communication and egocentric concerns. Given that we have at least some evidence of C\u2019s ability to work effectively with the crew\u2014a non\u2011negotiable safety factor\u2014I would shift my provisional recommendation to **Candidate\u202fC**."}
